  "primary_conclusions": [
    "Always selecting the highest accepted/admissible reference is rejected by controlled synthetic truth: it repeatedly selected about 24.47 km and produced larger lower-column errors than minimum-Rayleigh-cost selection.",
    "Minimum existing Rayleigh diagnostic cost after QA and path admissibility is retained as the first method-v5 selector architecture; no new molecular-purity score is introduced.",
    "No tested fixed lower altitude (8, 10 or 12 km) guarantees molecular purity. Broad smooth aerosol contamination can make a different floor appear preferable when the contamination altitude is moved.",
    "The first prototype uses 10 km as a configurable search-domain lower bound, not as an aerosol-free criterion. Residual boundary aerosol sensitivity remains mandatory.",
    "The 355/532 cross-wavelength synthetic comparison normalizes noise to each synthetic wavelength and therefore tests algorithmic behavior, not the real detector/noise difference between SPU channels."
  ],
